Maybe. Though, in my (surely limited) experience, I had more problems
with folks on WinDOS platforms who thought to have to program (or did
not know better) non-standard MS C++, than having problems with the
C++ standard itself. Pre-STL there were more problems, but primarily
with the build process, or with a non-standard zoo of libraries, less
with the language itself. But, frankly, in the C++ projects were I had
been involved (as head or coder) we were very careful; we had our test
environment on all platforms we delivered for, turned compiler warning
levels to a high value, made code reviews as quality assurance means,
and had own standards to support writing portable code.

>>[...]
